    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a bridge for me—both as a subject I struggled through and one that fascinated me in its precision. My parents taught it through rote memorization, but my curiosity led me to explore physics later, where equations became tangible. Now, as someone who values logic over abstract concepts, math feels like a tool rather than an end. It’s practical for problem-solving, even if I don’t always enjoy the process.",
